CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 2 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --no-assertions --datarace
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
Builds on `if_condition_read_race`: a `_Bool` element is one byte wide, so
reading it as a value (inside `if (flags[0]) ...`) goes through an explicit
byte extraction on top of the if-condition shape that fix already handled:
`byte_extract(obj[k], 0, c_bool[8]) != 0`, not a bare `obj[k]` under the
comparison. `with_index_under_if` had no case for
`ID_byte_extract_little_endian`/`_big_endian`, so it never recursed into
the object being extracted from to find the nested index.

Reproducer: a symbolic-size malloc'd `_Bool` array, written unprotected in
main, read inside `if (flags[0])` under a mutex that only the reader holds
(still racy). Reported SUCCESSFUL before this fix, FAILED after.

See `bool_byte_extract_read_race_ordered`, the negative control: same
shape but the write happens-before the reader thread is created (and is
itself mutex-protected), so there is no race -- must stay SUCCESSFUL before
and after.
